  "summary": "I added Red, Blue and Black buttons in a row below the canvas, and `window.__TASK_STATE__` now includes `paintColor` ('red' | 'blue' | 'black'), starting at 'red'. Typecheck passes and the render shows the buttons under the canvas with Red highlighted. I could not click the buttons in the render tool, so the repaint itself is untested. I didn't check whether the new colours look right.\n\nClicking a button replaces the body and roof materials with a copy of the paint material that has only `color` changed. The clear coat, roughness, flake normal map, chrome and glass settings stay the same. The colours are `#6c000e` for red, `#0a2a8c` for blue and `#040406` for black. The change is in `src/main.ts`.\n\nBlue is deep blue but not literally more metallic than red, because I changed only the base colour as requested. The pressed button gets a white outline and `aria-pressed`, and `paintColor` updates on every click."
